# A shell script that runs inside a Linux container must leave this machine
# with LF endings whatever core.autocrlf says: a CR after the shebang is
# "bad interpreter" in the container, and `az acr build` uploads the working
# tree as it is on disk.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Font files are binary. autocrlf must never touch them: one rewritten byte
# and the browser silently falls back to the system face.
*.woff2 binary
